+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Respondent ids are case-insensitive: response files are read with ids in upper case, so `ab12` and `AB12` are one respondent.
 - Frequency tables list choice options in questionnaire order rather than from most to least chosen, so questions sharing an answer list line up.
 - Scale questions are called `rating` in survey files, as form builders name them; files that say `scale` still load.
 - Fixed: percentages in exported tables rounded halves to the even digit (1 of 8 showed as 12%); they now round half up.
